From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:13:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Split the eDP lanes between DDI-A and
 DDI-E

The VBT has a DisplayPort on DDI-E, but coreboot sets DDI_A_4_LANES,
which leaves DDI-E no lanes: i915 warns with a backtrace at every boot
("Not enough lanes (0) for DP on [ENCODER:140:DDI E/PHY E]") and gives
the port no connector. The board has no eDP panel on DDI-A. The OEM
firmware has a DP on DDI-E in the VBTs of some configurations of the
optional rear port, where it most likely feeds the DP-to-VGA adapter of
the VGA option. Select SOC_INTEL_GFX_ENABLE_DDI_E_BIFURCATION, so that
DDI-A and DDI-E get two lanes each.

TEST=On an M920x running the build before this, DDI_BUF_CTL_A reads
0x00000090, with DDI_A_4_LANES, i915 warns as above, and SFUSE_STRAP
shows DDI-B, DDI-C and DDI-D present; HDMI, on one of those, works in
the firmware. Built lenovo/m920x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
index f733c132ad..159820afb2 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ config BOARD_SPECIFIC_OPTIONS
 	select SOC_INTEL_CANNONLAKE_PCH_H
 	select SOC_INTEL_COFFEELAKE
 	select SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_HDA_VERB
+	select SOC_INTEL_GFX_ENABLE_DDI_E_BIFURCATION
 	select SUPERIO_NUVOTON_NCT6687D
 
 config MAINBOARD_DIR
